---
// The course-level mark for SLOP3092, used as the closing slide of every deck.
// It sits ALONGSIDE Slop University's crest, never in place of it: the crest is
// the institution's and arrives from astro-theme-slop, so `logo`, `logoDark`,
// `logoCompact` and `favicon` are untouched by this file (a deck page still
// carries the crest as its favicon, set in astro.config.ts).
//
// What it depicts: one retry glyph printed twice, the second impression offset
// like a misregistered press run — the retry that charged you again. Week 2's
// deck is "Charging twice on purpose", so this restates the course's argument
// rather than decorating it.
//
// Every number below is measured off astro-theme-slop's slop-crest.svg so the
// two marks read as the same hand:
//
//   stroke-width 1.644     identical to the crest's, and literal here because
//                          it scales with the group transform
//   4.535                  the crest's grid pitch (the spacing of its three
//                          steam plumes). The offset between the two
//                          impressions, and the length of each arrow barb.
//   46-unit canvas         the glyph is authored on the crest's own square and
//                          placed with one transform
//   fill none, round caps  identical; the crest is a single unfilled path
//
// The offset is horizontal, on one axis, because a press misregisters along
// the feed direction — and because the first cut offset it diagonally and
// that was worse on screen: the second impression's arrowhead landed behind
// the first impression's arc, so the ghost lost the one feature that showed
// it was the SAME glyph and the pair read as two unrelated rings. Offset on
// x alone, both arrowheads and both tails stay visible and the doubling is
// what you see first. Checked in a browser at 1280x720, not reasoned about.
//
// The frame is geometry rather than drawing, so the two rules are filled rects
// with `rx` echoing the round caps, not stroked paths — a stroked line has a
// zero-height fill box, and `transform-box: fill-box` below needs a real one.
//
// Layout and motion both come from astro-theme-university's deck.css
// (`.logo-slide`, `.logo-svg`, `.logo-group`, `.logo-rule-top`,
// `.logo-rule-bottom`), which was already styled, print-hardened and
// reduced-motion-aware but unused. Nothing here adds CSS. Two consequences:
//
//   * astromotion fixes Reveal's canvas at 1280x720 with `margin: 0`, so this
//     viewBox fills the slide exactly, with no letterboxing.
//   * deck.css animates the rules with `scaleY`, and on an SVG child
//     `transform-origin: 50% 50%` resolves against the VIEW BOX, not the
//     element — so without `transform-box: fill-box` a rule would collapse
//     toward the middle of the slide instead of growing where it sits.
//
// Colour is read from the brand tokens, never copied: bronze `--at-secondary`
// is drawn first, so the gold `--at-primary` original lands on top of it and
// the ghost stays the dimmer second impression (2.97:1 against the slide's
// #0d0d0d, to gold's 4.86:1 — deliberate, not an oversight).
const glyph =
  "M9.844 18.212A14 14 0 1 0 25.431 9.213M28.905 12.128 25.431 9.213 29.693 7.661";
---

<svg
  class="logo-svg"
  viewBox="0 0 1280 720"
  role="img"
  aria-labelledby="course-mark-title"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
  <title id="course-mark-title">
    SLOP3092 Try Again, Later: a retry glyph printed twice, the second
    impression offset like a misregistered press run
  </title>

  <rect
    class="logo-rule-top"
    x="120"
    y="92"
    width="1040"
    height="10"
    rx="5"
    fill="var(--at-tertiary)"
    style="transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: center"
  />

  <g
    class="logo-group"
    transform="translate(412.595 159.024) scale(9)"
    fill="none"
    stroke-width="1.644"
    stroke-linecap="round"
    stroke-linejoin="round"
  >
    <path d={glyph} transform="translate(4.535 0)" style="stroke: var(--at-secondary)" />
    <path d={glyph} style="stroke: var(--at-primary)" />
  </g>

  <rect
    class="logo-rule-bottom"
    x="120"
    y="618"
    width="1040"
    height="10"
    rx="5"
    fill="var(--at-tertiary)"
    style="transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: center"
  />
</svg>
